\ `evaluate` and deferred words resume the word that ran them.
\
\ Both re-enter the interpreter from inside a running word, and each used
\ to reload the caller's instruction pointer from ff->ip after the nested
\ run - which always leaves it NULL. `evaluate` crashed on every use; a
\ call to a deferred word silently ended the word that made it.

"1 2 +" evaluate . . cr                  \ 03: the error code 0, then 3
: t "3 4 *" evaluate drop 1 + . cr ;
t                                        \ 13
: nested "\"5 6 +\" evaluate drop" evaluate drop . cr ;
nested                                   \ 11

defer d
: seven 7 . ;
' seven is d
: x d 99 . cr ;
x                                        \ 799
: twice d d 1 . cr ;
twice                                    \ 771
